 "_doc": "Room styles (tools/room/lamplight/gi.py, rig.py). Changing a style's look is editing this file and re-running tools/room/build.sh: no code change. Space: metres, x right, y into the room, z up (scene.py). Per style: textures (its texture set); gi: the Cycles bake (lights: SUN/POINT/AREA with colour, power, pos, aim, size/radius/angle; exposure and gamma: irradiance to display light (gi.tone); range: the light range, 2 (PS1 x2) or 4; ao, ao_dist: the contact-shadow pass; emit/translucent: the shade's material; a light's only/except: [part names] it lights directly (light linking: the window's sun and sky on the wallpaper are their own, warmer and weaker, lights); samples, ao_samples: Cycles samples per vertex: the bake is bit-exact only for the same Blender build and counts). tint: flat colours of untextured parts. emit: self-light of the lamp shade and the candle on top of the bake. glow: additive halo per sprite key (colour, scale; absent = off). post: [dither strength 0..1, share of empty cubbies with decor 0..1]. texture_sets: each style's \"textures\" names one: wood, floor, wallpaper and rug palettes, the window gradient (sky) and the window view (sky_view); the patterns are the calm ones of light round 3 (tex.py); each set is its own 256x128 atlas. The light is V3 of light round 3 (owner approved 2026-11-07). Day neutral round: Day 2 Nov 7 colours with depth from the window; Night 2 moodier.",
